# print(sumOf(kept));
# -- end of source
# `checked` and `area` are copied in line. What runs other code in the copy is the construction of the RangeError, on a way that throws: no turn that comes round passes it. The row books that code under the call of the
# loop's own body, which does come round; whether the typed build is left on a usual way is seen where it is walked: it is not, so the loop keeps both builds.
# RUN: walk f3 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: 880
